#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:17
msgid ""
"The host runtime does not link `libcuda` at build time. The shared `cuda-"
"bindings` crate loads it at the first driver call, so a binary starts "
"without a driver and fails on that call with `CUDA_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED`; "
"the error message names the library files the loader tried. A driver whose "
"CUDA major version is older than the toolkit's (a 12.x driver with a 13.x "
"build) fails the same way with a \"driver too old\" message. | "
"**Rust**         | Nightly (pinned)    | Pinned in `cuda-oxide/rust-"
"toolchain.toml`                    |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:26
msgid "cuda-oxide currently targets **Linux only**. Windows is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:31
msgid "Dev Container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:33
msgid ""
"The repository includes a cuda-oxide devcontainer in `cuda-oxide/."
"devcontainer/`. Using it is the quickest way to get a reproducible "
"development environment with CUDA Toolkit 13.0, LLVM 21, Clang 21, and the "
"pinned Rust nightly already installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:38
msgid "The host does not need the CUDA Toolkit installed. It does need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:40
msgid "an NVIDIA GPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:41
msgid "an NVIDIA driver compatible with CUDA 13.0 (R580 or newer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:42
msgid "Docker with the NVIDIA Container Toolkit installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:44
msgid ""
"With a devcontainer-aware editor, open the checkout's `cuda-oxide/` folder "
"and choose \"Reopen in Container\". The editor reads its `.devcontainer/"
"devcontainer.json`, builds the image, and requests GPU access with `--"
"gpus=all`. The container mounts the whole repository so the shared host "
"crates remain available, and opens `/workspaces/cuda-rust/cuda-oxide`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:50
msgid "For CLI-only usage, run from the repository root:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:52
msgid ""
"npx -y @devcontainers/cli up --workspace-folder ./cuda-oxide \\\n"
"  --config ./cuda-oxide/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:57
msgid "Then run commands inside it with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:59
msgid ""
"npx -y @devcontainers/cli exec --workspace-folder ./cuda-oxide \\\n"
"  --config ./cuda-oxide/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json cargo oxide doctor\n"
"npx -y @devcontainers/cli exec --workspace-folder ./cuda-oxide \\\n"
"  --config ./cuda-oxide/.devcontainer/devcontainer.json cargo oxide run "
"vecadd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:66
msgid ""
"If the host driver is too old, GPU commands such as `nvidia-smi`, `cargo "
"oxide doctor`, or `cargo oxide run vecadd` will fail inside the container. "
"Update the host NVIDIA driver rather than installing a different CUDA "
"Toolkit in the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:71
msgid ""
"If you use the devcontainer, you can skip the manual CUDA, LLVM, Clang, and "
"Rust setup sections below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:76
msgid "Nix / flake.nix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:78
msgid ""
"The repository also ships `cuda-oxide/flake.nix`, providing a reproducible "
"dev shell (CUDA 13, LLVM 22, Clang, pinned Rust nightly). Requires [Nix]"
"(https://nixos.org/download/) with flakes enabled, an NVIDIA driver on the "
"host, and Linux (x86\\_64 or aarch64)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:83
msgid ""
"From the repository root, enter the cuda-oxide workspace; `cargo-oxide` is "
"included in the shell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:85
msgid ""
"cd cuda-oxide\n"
"nix develop\n"
"cargo oxide run vecadd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:91
msgid "To bootstrap a new project without cloning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:93
msgid ""
"nix run 'github:NVIDIA/cuda-rust?dir=cuda-oxide#new' -- my-project\n"
"cd my-project && nix develop\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:98
msgid ""
"This scaffolds via `cargo oxide new` and drops in a `flake.nix` that "
"inherits this repo's dev shell. The shellHook auto-discovers host NVIDIA "
"driver libraries on NixOS and non-NixOS systems; if the host driver is too "
"old, update it rather than changing what's inside the Nix shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:103
msgid ""
"To add the same development environment to an existing project, run inside "
"that project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:106
msgid ""
"nix flake init -t 'github:NVIDIA/cuda-rust?dir=cuda-oxide'\n"
"nix develop\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:111
msgid ""
"If you use the Nix flake, you can skip the manual CUDA, LLVM, Clang, and "
"Rust setup sections below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:116
msgid "CUDA Toolkit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:118
msgid ""
"Install the CUDA Toolkit from the [NVIDIA CUDA Downloads](https://developer."
"nvidia.com/cuda-downloads) page, then make sure it is on your `PATH`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:120
msgid "export PATH=\"/usr/local/cuda/bin:$PATH\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:124
msgid "Verify the install:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:126
msgid "nvcc --version\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:131
msgid ""
"If you installed CUDA to a non-default location, set `CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH` to "
"its root directory (the one containing `include/cuda.h`). If neither "
"`CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH` nor `CUDA_HOME` is set, these roots are tried in order "
"and the first one holding a `cuda.h` of CUDA 13.0 or newer wins: `/usr/local/"
"cuda-13.3`, `/usr/local/cuda-13.2`, `/usr/local/cuda-13`, `/usr/local/cuda`. "
"With more than one toolkit installed, that order decides — not the highest "
"version, and not the `/usr/local/cuda` symlink, which is last. `cargo oxide "
"doctor` reports which root it resolved and why any earlier one was turned "
"down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:136
msgid "Toolkit and driver compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:138
msgid ""
"The CUDA toolkit and NVIDIA driver are separate installations. A newer "
"toolkit can often run with an older driver through CUDA minor-version "
"compatibility, but that compatibility does not cover newer PTX:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:142
msgid ""
"cubin ───────────────────────────► driver loads finished GPU code\n"
"PTX   ──► driver compiles it ─────► finished GPU code\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:147
msgid ""
"The normal cuda-oxide path gets PTX from LLVM `llc`, so installing a newer "
"CUDA toolkit does not by itself change that PTX version. The NVVM forward-"
"execution path gets PTX from the selected toolkit's nvJitLink. If that PTX "
"is newer than the driver understands, module loading returns "
"`CUDA_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_PTX_VERSION` (error 222)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:153
msgid "For example, the toolchains used during current validation produced:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:155
msgid ""
"LLVM llc ───────────────► PTX 8.7 ──► driver 580 ✓\n"
"CUDA 13.3 nvJitLink ───► PTX 9.3 ──► driver 580 ✗ error 222\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:160
msgid ""
"These are observed versions, not permanent properties of the two paths. "
"Check the generated PTX `.version` directive when diagnosing another "
"toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:163
msgid ""
"CUDA 13.x minor-version compatibility starts at driver 580, while CUDA "
"13.3's corresponding full-support driver is 610.43.02. A 580 driver can "
"therefore load compatible finished cubins, but it cannot JIT PTX 9.3 "
"produced by CUDA 13.3. See the [CUDA release notes](https://docs.nvidia.com/"
"cuda/cuda-toolkit-release-notes/index.html) for the current driver table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:169
msgid "Upgrade the driver or select a compatible toolkit for the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:171
msgid ""
"CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH=/usr/local/cuda-13.0 cargo oxide run <example> --arch "
"sm_86\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:175
msgid ""
"See NVIDIA's [minor-version compatibility guide](https://docs.nvidia.com/"
"deploy/cuda-compatibility/minor-version-compatibility.html) for the "
"supported driver ranges and PTX limitation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:181
msgid "LLVM 21+ (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:183
msgid "cuda-oxide uses LLVM's NVPTX backend to lower LLVM IR to PTX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:185
msgid "Usually `llc` in Rust toolchain is enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:187
msgid ""
"Install LLVM 21 or newer and make sure `llc-21` (or `llc-22`) is on your "
"`PATH`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:189
msgid ""
"# Ubuntu / Debian\n"
"sudo apt install llvm-21\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:194
msgid ""
"If your distro packages do not provide `llvm-21`, use LLVM's apt helper:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:196
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get install -y lsb-release wget software-properties-common gnupg\n"
"wget https://apt.llvm.org/llvm.sh && chmod +x llvm.sh\n"
"sudo ./llvm.sh 21\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:202
msgid "Verify that the NVPTX target is present:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:204
msgid "llc-21 --version | grep nvptx\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:208
msgid ""
"You should see a line containing `nvptx64` in the registered targets. The "
"pipeline auto-discovers `llc-23`, `llc-22`, and `llc-21` in that order; pin "
"a specific binary with `CUDA_OXIDE_LLC=/usr/bin/llc-21` if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:213
msgid ""
"A stock LLVM build without the NVPTX backend will not work. The `llvm-21` "
"Ubuntu package includes it by default, but if you build LLVM from source you "
"must pass `-DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=\"X86;NVPTX\"` to CMake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:217
msgid ""
"**Why LLVM 21?** We emit TMA / tcgen05 / WGMMA intrinsics that `llc` from "
"LLVM 20 and earlier can't handle. Simple kernels might still work with an "
"older `llc` (set `CUDA_OXIDE_LLC=/path/to/llc-20`), but anything Hopper / "
"Blackwell needs 21+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:222
msgid "Clang (host `cuda-bindings`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:224
msgid ""
"The host `cuda-bindings` crate runs [`bindgen`](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rust-bindgen), which loads `libclang.so` at runtime and needs clang's own "
"resource-dir `stddef.h` — a bare `libclang1-*` runtime is not enough. Three "
"packages cover both halves:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:226
msgid ""
"sudo apt install libclang-21-dev libclang-cpp21-dev libclang-common-21-dev\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:230
msgid ""
"`cargo oxide doctor` catches this up front; the symptom otherwise is "
"`'stddef.h' file not found` during the host build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:233
msgid ""
"**If doctor still reports clang not found:** The issue may be that the "
"versioned binary (e.g., clang-21) is installed but not mapped to the "
"unversioned clang command required by bindgen. You can fix this by "
"installing the clang meta-package, which manages these dependencies "
"automatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:236
msgid "sudo apt install clang libclang-dev\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:243
msgid ""
"**Fresh Ubuntu 24.04 / DGX-OS:** after installing LLVM 21 via `apt.llvm.org/"
"llvm.sh` as shown above, the versioned `clang-21` / `clang++-21` binaries "
"are present but the unversioned aliases `cargo oxide doctor` looks for are "
"not. Add them with `update-alternatives`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:245
msgid ""
"sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/clang   clang   /usr/bin/"
"clang-21   100\n"
"sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/clang++ clang++ /usr/bin/clang+"
"+-21 100\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:250
msgid "Validated on Asus GX10 / NVIDIA DGX Spark."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:255
msgid "Rust toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:257
msgid ""
"The CUDA Oxide workspace ships `cuda-oxide/rust-toolchain.toml`, which pins "
"the exact nightly version and required components. When you first run a "
"`cargo` command inside `cuda-oxide/`, rustup installs the correct toolchain "
"automatically. Commands at the repository root and in `cutile-rs/` use "
"stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:262
msgid "If you need to install it manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:264
msgid ""
"rustup toolchain install nightly-2026-10-11\n"
"rustup component add rust-src rustc-dev rust-analyzer clippy rustfmt llvm-"
"tools --toolchain nightly-2026-10-11\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:269
msgid "Three of these components are what the codegen backend and doctor need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:271
msgid ""
"`rust-src` -- source of the Rust standard library, needed for cross-"
"compiling to the NVPTX target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:272
msgid "`rustc-dev` -- compiler internals that the backend links against."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:273
msgid ""
"`llvm-tools` -- toolchain-bundled `llc` used to lower LLVM IR to PTX "
"(doctor's floor check)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:275
msgid ""
"The other three are not needed to build: `rust-analyzer` powers IDE support, "
"`clippy` is the lint gate CI runs, and `rustfmt` backs `cargo oxide fmt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:279
msgid "cargo-oxide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:281
msgid ""
"`cargo-oxide` is the cargo subcommand that drives the entire build pipeline "
"(`cargo oxide run`, `build`, `debug`, `pipeline`, and the rest -- the "
"Command reference at the end of this section lists all of them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:283
msgid ""
"**Inside the cuda-oxide repo**, it works out of the box via a workspace "
"alias -- no extra install step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:285
msgid ""
"**For use outside the repo** (your own projects), install it with the pinned "
"nightly toolchain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:287
msgid ""
"cargo +nightly-2026-10-11 install --git https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust."
"git cargo-oxide\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:291
msgid ""
"On first run, `cargo-oxide` will automatically fetch and build the codegen "
"backend. Subsequent runs reuse the cached build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:293
msgid "To discover the examples available in a cuda-oxide checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:295
msgid ""
"cargo oxide list\n"
"cargo oxide list --json\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:300
msgid ""
"The command reports each example's purpose and any documented GPU, "
"architecture, CUDA Toolkit, or external SDK requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:303
msgid "Useful day-to-day helpers once you are building kernels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:305
msgid ""
"# Print generated PTX without the full MIR/LLVM pipeline dump\n"
"cargo oxide inspect vecadd\n"
"\n"
"# Remove local target/ dirs and generated device artifacts (PTX, LLVM IR,\n"
"# LTOIR, cubin, and their sidecar metadata)\n"
"cargo oxide clean\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../getting-started/installation.md:314
msgid ""
"`inspect` is the lightweight counterpart to `cargo oxide pipeline`. `clean` "
"only touches project-local outputs; it leaves the shared backend cache at "
"`~/.cargo/cuda-oxide/` alone."
msgstr ""

